"]}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Prompting"}]]}],["$","span","prompt-anatomy",{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-right size-3.5","aria-hidden":"true","children":[["$","path","mthhwq",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-foreground","children":"Prompt Anatomy"}]]}]]]}],["$","header",null,{"className":"mb-10 border-b border-border pb-8","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-balance text-4xl font-bold tracking-[-0.035em] sm:text-5xl","children":"Anatomy of a strong prompt"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 max-w-2xl text-pretty text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"A repeatable structure for specifying the audience, workflow, states, content, and visual direction of an app."}]]}],null,["$","article",null,{"className":"docs-prose prose prose-zinc max-w-none dark:prose-invert prose-headings:font-semibold prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-h2:mt-14 prose-h2:border-t prose-h2:border-border prose-h2:pt-10 prose-h3:mt-9 prose-p:leading-7 prose-a:font-medium prose-a:text-primary prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline prose-strong:text-foreground prose-code:before:content-none prose-code:after:content-none prose-pre:my-7 prose-pre:overflow-x-auto prose-pre:rounded-xl prose-pre:border prose-pre:border-border prose-pre:bg-zinc-950 prose-pre:p-4 prose-pre:text-zinc-100 prose-li:my-1.5 prose-hr:border-border","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"The goal is not to make a prompt long. The goal is to remove ambiguity from the product decisions that matter."}],"\n",["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"1-name-the-audience-and-job","children":"1. Name the audience and job"}],"\n","$L3","\n","$L4","\n","$L5","\n","$L6","\n","$L7","\n","$L8","\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15"]}],"$L16"]}],"$L17"]}],["$L18"],"$L19"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"q2m7bQIiF_hArhhzVxdCC"}
3:["$","p",null,{"children":"“Build a dashboard” leaves both the data and decisions undefined. “Build a morning operations dashboard for a regional delivery manager” gives the interface a real point of view."}]
4:["$","p",null,{"children":"State the primary job as a verb: triage, schedule, compare, approve, publish, review, or track."}]
5:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"2-list-essential-regions","children":"2. List essential regions"}]
6:["$","p",null,{"children":"Describe screens or regions by their purpose:"}]
7:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"A queue for work that needs attention."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"A detail view with enough context to make a decision."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Filters that match how the audience thinks about the data."}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"A success state that confirms what changed."}],"\n"]}]
8:["$","p",null,{"children":"This is more durable than micromanaging containers and grid columns."}]
9:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"3-specify-interactions-and-states","children":"3. Specify interactions and states"}]
a:["$","p",null,{"children":"If a control must work, say what it changes. Include the non-happy states that make the surface feel complete."}]
b:["$","$L1a",null,{"title":"Interaction requirements","text":"The status filter must update the visible jobs and result count. Selecting a row opens its detail panel without losing the current filters. Saving a reassignment should update the row, show a brief confirmation, and preserve the selected job. Include a useful no-results state and a disabled save state when nothing changed."}]
c:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"4-give-visual-direction-with-evidence","children":"4. Give visual direction with evidence"}]
d:["$","p",null,{"children":"Use concrete qualities that affect implementation:"}]
e:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Dense or spacious"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Editorial or utilitarian"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"High-contrast or quiet"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Sharp or rounded"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Image-led or data-led"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"One accent color or a broader semantic palette"}],"\n"]}]
f:["$","p",null,{"children":"If you provide a visual reference, explain which parts matter. A screenshot can guide layout and styling, but your text should still define the desired product behavior."}]
10:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"5-protect-the-scope","children":"5. Protect the scope"}]
11:["$","p",null,{"children":"End with the priority and important exclusions."}]
12:["$","$L1a",null,{"title":"Complete prompt","text":"Build a shift handoff workspace for charge nurses in a 24-bed hospital unit.\n\nThe primary job is to review unresolved patient-care tasks before accepting the next shift.\n\nInclude:\n\n- A unit overview with bed number, patient initials, acuity, and outstanding task count\n- Filters for acuity, task owner, and overdue status\n- A patient detail drawer with task history, notes, and a clear accept-handoff action\n- Selected, loading, no-results, validation, and success states\n- Realistic but fictional sample data with no sensitive information\n\nThe filters must update the visible rows and counts. Opening and closing the detail drawer must preserve the current filters. Accepting a handoff should update the patient row and show a confirmation.\n\nUse a calm, high-clarity clinical interface with compact spacing, strong type hierarchy, restrained blue and teal accents, and accessible contrast. Prioritize the handoff workflow over analytics, settings, or marketing content."}]
13:["$","h2",null,{"className":"scroll-mt-24","id":"a-quick-self-review","children":"A quick self-review"}]
14:["$","p",null,{"children":"Before submitting, ask:"}]
15:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Is there one primary user and one primary job?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Did I name the data that drives the screen?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Did I say which interactions must work?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Did I include at least one non-happy state?"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Is the visual direction specific without prescribing every CSS decision?"}],"\n"]}]
